      <description>&lt;p&gt;I grabbed the openSUSE 11.4 64-bit ISO last night and spent the afternoon installing it in a VM. Here&amp;rsquo;s the full walkthrough, screenshots and all.&lt;/p&gt;





  
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.shafiq.in/wp-content/uploads/2011/03/opensuse-64-bit-2011-03-13-10-33-52_hu_9afb819bd014bb41.png&#34; alt=&#34;OpenSUSE installer boot menu&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; decoding=&#34;async&#34; class=&#34;&#34; /&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Boot menu. Standard options &amp;ndash; Installation, Rescue System, media check. Nothing fancy, but it gets the job done.&lt;/p&gt;





  
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.shafiq.in/wp-content/uploads/2011/03/opensuse-64-bit-2011-03-13-10-36-48_hu_d42add61d7477477.png&#34; alt=&#34;ISOLINUX boot screen&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; decoding=&#34;async&#34; class=&#34;&#34; /&gt;







  
  &lt;img src=&#34;https://www.shafiq.in/wp-content/uploads/2011/03/opensuse-64-bit-2011-03-13-10-36-51_hu_15701d2a0de05fc.png&#34; alt=&#34;OpenSUSE welcome screen with CD graphic&#34; loading=&#34;lazy&#34; decoding=&#34;async&#34; class=&#34;&#34; /&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Welcome screen. The green chameleon is back, and so is the striped wallpaper that&amp;rsquo;s become the distro&amp;rsquo;s signature look.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
